### Guide §5.6 Transactions. VS Code REST Client syntax: click "Send Request" above each request.
### Start the app with the dev profile (demo authors, books, members and loans):
###   ./mvnw -pl spring-app spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.profiles=dev
### Ids and statuses assume the demo data on an empty database, and a first run of this file: reset
### with docker compose -f spring-app/compose.yaml down -v
### The races themselves need two requests at the same moment, which this file cannot send:
### LoanConcurrencyIT forces them. Here, watch the SQL in the console instead.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Alan has the only copy of The Dispossessed, so Ada's borrow is refused (409). The borrow's
### transaction rolls back. Before that, the console shows an insert into audit_events: it ran in a
### transaction of its own (REQUIRES_NEW), already committed
POST {{host}}/api/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{"bookId": 4, "memberId": 1}

### The audit trail, newest first (200): the refused borrow is there, the loan is not
GET {{host}}/api/audit-events

### Alan borrows Cosmos (201). At commit the console shows the two forced version bumps
###   update books set version=? where id=? and version=?
###   update members set version=? where id=? and version=?
### A second borrow of Cosmos, or a second borrow by Alan, racing this one would match no row (409)
# @name loan
POST {{host}}/api/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{"bookId": 8, "memberId": 2}

### Return it (200). The UPDATE of the loan ends with "where id=? and version=?" (@Version on Loan)
POST {{host}}/api/loans/{{loan.response.body.id}}/return

### Return it again (409, "... was already returned"): the check, not the lock, since the first
### return committed long ago
POST {{host}}/api/loans/{{loan.response.body.id}}/return

### An edit bumps the version as well: "update books set ..., version=? where id=? and version=?".
### A borrow of Cosmos racing this edit collides with it: whichever commits second gets a 409.
### Alone, the edit is a 200
PUT {{host}}/api/books/8
Content-Type: application/json

{"isbn": "9780345539434", "title": "Cosmos", "publishedYear": 1980, "totalCopies": 3, "authorIds": [4]}

### Four events (200): two returns, two borrows, rejected or not
GET {{host}}/api/audit-events
